\begin{lem}
$H_0$ is a closed subspace of $H$.
\end{lem}
\begin{proof}
As we have noted in Theorem \ref{th::3}, the trace of functions in $H$ is a well defined function in $H^{\frac{1}{2}}(\mathbb R)$. In particular, the trace mapping $T:H\to L^2(\mathbb R)$ is continuous by Sobolev embedding (Theorem \ref{Sobolev}). Then, if we have a sequence $\{u_k\}_{k=1}^\infty\to u_0$ in $H$ with $u_k\in H_0$, then
$$\abs{\int_{\partial\Omega} \phi'(u_k-u_0)}\leq \left(\int_{\partial\Omega} \phi'^2\right)^{1/2} \left(\int_{\partial\Omega} \abs{u_k-u_0}^2\right)^{1/2}\to 0\quad\mbox{when } k\to \infty,$$
using the bounds for $\phi'$ given in \eqref{asymptotics}.
We conclude that $u_0\in H_0$, and the lemma is shown.
\end{proof}
\qed

