We now quote the regularity theory for bounded weak solutions of \cite{Cabre-SolaMorales:layer-solutions}.

\begin{pro}{\bf (Regularity of weak solutions)}. \label{prop-regularity}
Let $R>0$, $\beta\in(0,1)$, and let $w\in H^{\frac{1}{2}}(\mathbb R)$ be a weak solution of \eqref{weak-equation} with $d\in\mathcal C^\beta([-4R,4R])$, $g\in\mathcal C^\beta([-4R,4R])$. If $u=P*_x w \in L^\infty (B^+_{4R})\cap W^{1,2}(B_{4R}^+)$, then $u\in \mathcal C^{1,\beta}(\overline{B_R^+})$ and
$$\norm{u}_{\mathcal C^{1,\beta}(\overline{B_R^+})}\leq C_R,$$
for some constant $C_R$ that depends only on $\beta$, $R$ and on the upper bounds for $\norm{u}_{L^\infty (B^+_{4R})}$, $\norm{d}_{\mathcal C^\beta([-4R,4R])}$ and $\norm{g}_{\mathcal C^\beta([-4R,4R])}$.
\end{pro}

\begin{proof}
This is a consequence of Lemma 2.3 from \cite{Cabre-SolaMorales:layer-solutions}, using  definition \ref{defi-weak-solution} for weak solutions.
\end{proof}
\qed


